# Keeps the build context small and the image honest. Unignored the context is
# over 3GB, and `COPY . .` would bake the host's node_modules and build output
# into the image instead of what `yarn install` produces inside it.
#
# Deliberately scoped to paths rather than `**/` globs: a blanket `**/generated`
# or `**/build` would also drop 96 tracked files of committed graph codegen
# under packages/subgraph*/generated. Nothing here excludes a tracked file, so
# the image holds the whole repo as git sees it, minus regenerable output.

.git
**/node_modules

# Vendored yarn lives in .yarn/releases and the Dockerfile needs it; the cache
# and unplugged trees are large and rebuildable.
.yarn/cache
.yarn/unplugged
.yarn/install-state.gz

# hardhat / foundry / typechain output. All untracked, all regenerated by the
# compile that hardhat runs at deploy time.
packages/contracts/generated
packages/contracts/artifacts
packages/contracts/cache
packages/contracts/out
packages/contracts/build
packages/contracts/coverage

# Never ship secrets into an image layer.
# The context is the working tree, not git, so a developer's real .env would
# otherwise be copied in. The two tracked templates are rescued explicitly.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.*.example
!**/.env.template
**/mnemonic.secret
**/*.secret
